# Everything here is OPTIONAL. To use it, copy this file to ".env" (note the leading dot).
# With no .env at all, the project runs local-only (plain HTTP on port 8080) with a generated password.
# Full instructions: README.md

# ---- Login ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The password you type on the car's touchscreen. Leave out to use a generated one
# (shown by "docker compose logs", also saved in data/password.txt).
# PASSWORD=pick-something-you-can-type

# ---- Online with HTTPS (needed for the Tesla browser) -----------------------------------
# Uncomment BOTH lines and set your own domain. Needs DNS + router ports 80 and 443 (see README step 3).
# DOMAIN=theatre.yourdomain.com
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.caddy.yml
#   ^ use ; instead of : between the two files on Windows.
# For local-only use, leave DOMAIN and COMPOSE_FILE out.

# ---- Where things live ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder with your shows/movies (mounted read-only).
# MEDIA_PATH=./media
# Watch progress, thumbnails and caches.
# DATA_PATH=./data

# ---- Tuning -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE_NAME=Charge Theatre
# Encoder used when a file must be transcoded:
#   libx264 (CPU, default) | h264_nvenc (NVIDIA) | h264_qsv (Intel) | h264_videotoolbox (Mac, no Docker)
# ENCODER=libx264
# X264_PRESET=veryfast      # slower = better compression, more CPU
# MAX_TRANSCODES=2          # simultaneous encodes
# SESSION_DAYS=90           # how long a sign-in lasts
